Subject: attention-gateway P3 — one door: lane posters route through the gated channel

GERMLINE CARRY NOTE: applies ON TOP of p1-action-lane-canonical-dedup.patch
and p2-acted-overlay-world-grounding.patch (sequential). Same carry
contract: authored from scratch copies, applied on-branch with `git apply`,
PR diff is the proposal, Captain merge = apply + live-checkout relock.

What it wires (spec §4.4 + §13 transport verdict):
- run_action_lane._tg and action_exec._tg_send stop posting raw to
  api.telegram.org and route through framework.frontdoor.channel.send —
  killswitch/allow_sends gate, token scrub, 4096 chunking, transport retry,
  and the P3 feed-journal row, with the same loud-failure contract
  (ANY non-sent status raises, INCLUDING blocked-dev — cp3 H1/H2: a
  production process missing CABINET_ENV=runtime must page, never silently
  blackhole cards while ledger rows record them as presented).
- Requires CABINET_ENV=runtime in the lane plists (added in the same
  commit, non-germline): without the runtime marker the allow_sends gate
  would silently block every card.
- Pinned by framework/tests/test_single_telegram_door.py (shrink-only
  allowlist; the kill-list files may never carry a raw call again).

Spec: docs/plans/cabinet-attention-gateway-spec-2026-07-08.md §8 P3.

